<<<
broke(n). The form broke, now obsolete or a blunder in most senses, is still idiomatic (1) as p.p. of break = dismiss the service (he was broke for cowardice) except in the attributive use (a broken officer), and (2) in the slang phrase stony-broke.
===
**broke(n).** The form *broke*, now obsolete or a blunder in most senses, is still idiomatic (1) as p.p. of *break* = dismiss the service (*he was broke for cowardice*) except in the attributive use (*a broken officer*), and (2) in the slang phrase *stony-broke*.
>>>

